{"type":"text","timestamp":1794304641214,"sessionID":"ses_e3b381c85ffehR025udqZemf3u","part":{"id":"prt_1c4e3f63a001VTiYYxlTRs62GA","sessionID":"ses_e3b381c85ffehR025udqZemf3u","messageID":"msg_1c4e3c194001hZ0JlO7tn22N2s","type":"text","text":"All 6 tests pass. The fix was a token type mismatch: the lexer emits `(\"COMMA\", \",\")` but the parser was checking for `(\"OP\", \",\")`. Changed the condition to `self.peek()[0] == \"COMMA\"` so it correctly recognizes commas between function call arguments.","time":{"start":1794304636474,"end":1794304641214}}}
